## Reviewer disagreements (not applied)
No wording was rejected as a wrong reading of the English. The five skipped rows are checker or pin constraints, not a disagreement about Serbian:

- sr-a 16. The reviewer is right that `flno=3` does not open article 10. The Korean and English labels still say article 10, and removing "član 10" drops a digit the checker requires. The label and the URL were left.
- sr-a 21 and sr-b 20. The blanks and the body-line Q16–Q20 are real, and they match the Korean source. Promoting them to headings or deleting U+200B fails the checker.
- sr-a 32. "jednog oštećenog" would be more natural. The Korean counters are parsed as the digit 1, so the digit stays.
- sr-a 35. "1,57 miliona TWD" is the Serbian form. The bio figure is pinned as "TWD 1.57M".
- sr-b 28 (and the same split in sr-a 12 and sr-b 6). Joining the paragraphs would change the block count. Each block was rephrased so it stands on its own.
